REGIONAL REGULATION OF BALANGAN REGENCY

NUMBER 3 OF 2016

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

REGENT OF BALANGAN,

Considering:

a. that every woman and child has the right to obtain protection of their human rights, freedom from torture, threats, pressure, as well as to receive equal facilities, treatment, opportunities and benefits in order to achieve justice and welfare of life;
b. that the improvement of the quality of life of women and children is a mandatory affair which is the responsibility of the Regional Government;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women From Acts of Violence;

In View of:

1. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
2. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
3. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection;
4. Law Number 2 of 2003 concerning Establishment of Tanah Bumbu Regency and Balangan Regency in the Province of South Kalimantan (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4265);
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
6. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
7. Law Number 44 of 2008 concerning Pornography (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 181, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4928);
8. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning Establishment of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as last amended by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
10. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);
11. Presidential Regulation Number 18 of 2014 concerning Protection And Empowerment of Women And Children In Social Conflict (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 44);
12. Presidential Regulation Number 69 of 2008 concerning Task Force for Prevention and Handling of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 02 of 2008 concerning Implementation of Women's Protection;
14. Regulation of the Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2009 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons;
15. Regional Regulation of South Kalimantan Province Number 9 of 2008 concerning Protection of Neglected Children (Regional Gazette of 2008 No.9);

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BALANGAN REGENCY

and

REGENT OF BALANGAN

DECIDES:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE.

CHAPTER III

SCOPE

Article 3

1. Every woman and child has the right to receive protection from acts of violence.
2. Acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) are in the form of acts of:
a. physical violence;
b. sexual violence;
c. psychological violence;
d. intimidation;
e. forced eviction;
f. deprivation of liberty;
g. neglect; and
h. exploitation, trafficking in persons.
3. Protection of women and children from acts of violence is the shared responsibility of the Regional Government, community, family, and parents.
4. Protection of women from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (2) includes:
a. prevention of acts of violence against women and children;
b. services for women and children who are victims of violence; and
c. empowerment of women and children who are victims of violence.

Article 5

1. The Regional Government in accordance with its authority carries out early prevention efforts.
2. Early prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are in the form of:
a. conducting data collection and assessment of conditions, fulfillment of rights and various aspects related to women and children in social life in the community;
b. mapping areas prone to acts of violence based on data collection and assessment as referred to in letter a and providing solutions in the form/manner capable of minimizing vulnerability;
c. increasing public legal awareness through the role of community institutions/customary institutions, interfaith communication forums to provide protection for women and children;
d. increasing the role of mass media in providing dissemination and information on the protection of women and children;
e. regular counseling or socialization of laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children;
f. opening channels for public complaints, and coordination channels from the village/sub-district, sub-district and Regional Government levels;
g. immediate handling of community reports.

CHAPTER V SERVICES

Article 6

1. The Regional Government provides services to women and children who are victims of violence and neglect.
2. Services as referred to in paragraph (1) are in the form of:
a. complaints;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. social reintegration; and
e. legal assistance and accompaniment.

BAB VI EMPOWERMENT

Article 8

1. The Regional Government in accordance with its authority empowers women and children victims of violence and neglect in the form of increasing life resilience and improving economic enterprises.
2. Increasing life resilience as referred to in paragraph (1) by providing guidance and assistance for mental spiritual strengthening in the form of religious knowledge.
3. Improving economic enterprises as referred to in paragraph (1) by providing:
a. work skills training;
b. productive economic enterprise training and joint business groups;
c. assistance in developing productive economic enterprises;
d. capital assistance; and
e. ease of access to information and marketing promotion of productive economic production results.

Article 14

1. The Management of the Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment (P2TP2A) consists of leadership and member elements stipulated by Regent's Decree.
2. Leadership elements include:
a. chairperson;
b. secretary; and
c. treasurer.
3. Membership elements are divided into the form of:
a. service division;
b. information division;
c. assistance division;
d. education and training division.

Article 15

1. The Center for Protection and Empowerment of Women and Children in carrying out its functions builds a working network with:
a. Police;
b. Prosecutor's Office;
c. Court;
d. Witness and Victim Protection Agency;
e. Hospital/Community Health Center;
f. Other institutions that have common objectives.
2. In addition to building a working network as referred to in paragraph (1), cooperation may be conducted with:
a. Government;
b. Provincial Government;
c. Other Regency/City Governments; and
d. Non-Governmental Institutions.
e. International institutions whose existence is recognized.
3. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), is set forth in the form of a joint agreement.

CHAPTER VIII

COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION

Article 18

1. The community may participate in providing protection and empowerment to women and children victims of violence, neglect and trafficking in persons.
2. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be in the form of:
a. providing information to authorized officials or institutions;
b. assisting in the rescue of women and children;
c. providing basic and or specific needs assistance for women and children;
d. forming family partners or small units in the village/sub-district environment that are actively together safeguarding the environment of women and children from violence;
e. independently socializing the rights of women and children;
f. providing legal assistance and accompaniment.
3. Community participation in providing protection and empowerment of women and children is carried out responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

CHAPTER IX

GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION

Article 19

1. The Regent conducts guidance and supervision of the organization of regional protection and empowerment of women and children.
2. The community is authorized to actively supervise the organization of regional protection and empowerment of women and children.
3. The authority of the community as referred to in paragraph (2) is in the form of:
a. providing input;
b. submitting questions and obtaining answers from responsible regional government officials;
c. requesting realization and real activities from those given duties and authority;
d. other matters that are constructive and provide solutions.
